
 fillawsusage - Fill table 'awsusage' from AWS Server log files.

 Reads AWS access logs from /gpfs/fs1/collections/rda/transfer/AWSera5log/
 and inserts usage records into the 'awsusage' table in PostgreSQL
 database 'rdadb'.

 USAGE:
   fillawsusage [-b] (-d LogFileDates | -N NumberDays | -p BeginDate [EndDate])

 OPTIONS (choose exactly one of -d, -N, or -p):

   -d LogFileDates
        Process log files for the given dates.
        Date format: YYYY-MM-DD (e.g. 2024-01-15).

   -N NumberDays
        Process log files covering the most recent NumberDays days.

   -p BeginDate [EndDate]
        Process log files between BeginDate and EndDate, inclusive.
        EndDate defaults to today if omitted.

   -b   Run in background mode (log to file only, no terminal output).

 EXAMPLE:
   fillawsusage -p 2024-01-01 2024-01-31
